WEBVTT

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.490
From that day on, I wondered if it was okay.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.280
I entrust Rea to you.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.630
After that disgusting father had entrusted Rea to me,

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.650
rather than feeling happy about setting Rea free,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.630
to be honest, I've realised the weight of this responsibility.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.060
Why on earth did someone put eggplants into the miso soup?

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.900
Grandpa, they are green peppers.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.400
Eh?

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.780
I see.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.030
Mero.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.910
What is it?

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:25.540
Rea-chan's meal is very special.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.370
I made Rea-dono's meal according to her tastes.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.420
A side dish of hydrangea leaves,

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.250
stir fried hydrangea leaves,

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.920
and soup of hydrangea leaves.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.430
Does that taste good?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.800
Even though I did everything that I could,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.560
there is still a limit.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.680
I told you that Rea is a vegetarian.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.310
Are hydrangea leaves vegetables?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.310
I'm sorry.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.860
As I thought, it would be better for me to have meals alone.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.570
No, I didn't mean it like that.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.530
Dad, don't push her so much.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.450
Sorry, I'm just a little surprised by the unusual meal.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.290
No, don't worry about it.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.050
Grandpa can be like this sometimes.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.720
If it happens, do this.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.590
O-Okay.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.720
Sorry for everything, Rea-chan.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.970
Not at all.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.650
I think they were just being courteous.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.230
Even though everyone apart from Grandpa is getting suspicious,

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.610
they don't ask questions out of kindness.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.820
More importantly, we're definitely family.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:48.080
Taking care of someone by yourself is really troublesome.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.500
Let alone a zombie.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.050
Hey.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:02.760
Eh?

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.260
Yes?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.280
To be honest, I want to take you to more places.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.860
Right.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.410
Sorry.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.490
I can't do much apart from this.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.250
That's not true.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.410
I'm having fun.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:36.420
When I was in my house, I couldn't even do something like this.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.460
Really?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.050
Yes.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.470
Furuya-kun.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.010
Eh?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.890
There's a fireworks display tomorrow, right?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.940
Ah that's right, they do one every year.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.190
I've never been to one before, though.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.070
Isn't it nice?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.400
As I gazed out from the window in my room,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.490
I've always thought about standing beneath it,
and watching it at least once.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.370
We'll go, then.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:12.950
Eh?

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.120
Is that okay?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.670
The fireworks display is at night, anyway.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.210
I'll take you to see it.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.290
Really?!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:24.840
All right, I'll do my very best to prepare
myself so that my body doesn't rot tomorrow.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.260
Why on earth would it suddenly rot?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.300
It can't be helped... It's only a fireworks display, yet it makes you so happy.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.850
Are you a kid?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.140
I am a kid!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.480
Do you have a problem with that?

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.230
Don't be so serious!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.490
A method to preserve Rea's body...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.740
Embalming and preservatives...

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.850
Even though I have investigated a lot,

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.240
I have not found an effective method.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.870
Of course that's right.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.660
A method to prevent a zombie from rotting...

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.460
No one would have thought about it before.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.140
Eh?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:01.920
Aren't you coming up?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.380
Yeah, in a bit.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.630
Grandpa is the only one I can rely on.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:16.270
What should I do to protect Rea and her everyday life?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.480
Nii, what are you doing?

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.820
Yeah, hold on...

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.110
By the way, do you not let Rea-dono go to school?

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.700
School?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.820
That's kind of impossible.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.660
Why is that?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.660
The reason is health related.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.750
There doesn't appear to be a problem from what I can see.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.500
That's only her appearance.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.500
However, there are a lot of things troubling her inside.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.260
This morning, when I was going to school, she told me this.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:53.100
"School, right? I'm jealous of you."

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.100
I see.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:01.310
If the disease only causes her to leave early every other day, she can still attend school.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:04.320
I've already thought about that.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.940
Then there must be a reason for you to keep Rea-dono inside all the time.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.570
That's right...

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:12.990
What can I do?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.990
How could I say that Rea's current way of life is normal?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.750
Could I say that she's a normal girl?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.500
Is her life too much for me to handle?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:31.020
As if reflecting my feelings,

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:34.260
the rain smashed any hopes for the fireworks display.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.760
Cancelled, huh?

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.970
I suppose it can't be helped.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.730
I'm sorry.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.480
What are you apologising for?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.230
I feel like I should.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.520
That doesn't make sense.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.280
If...

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.280
If I manage to stay alive,

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.280
please take me next year.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.910
It's a promise.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.300
Since the fireworks display was cancelled,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.430
we missed out on encountering a group of beautiful girls wearing yukatas, you know?

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.750
For a pure hearted high school student like myself,

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:21.810
life has seriously lost some of its meaning. And you?

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.730
Yasutaka-kun, you're fine with anyone as long as she's a girl.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.440
Why you...  I wasn't saying that.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.780
This so called... What is it?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.740
Furuya, you too?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.780
What?

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.120
Are you imagining the Sanjou girls wearing yukatas?

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.620
No, you pervert.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.370
Chihiro.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.710
Good morning!

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.710
Ah, Ranko.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.920
What are you doing with that idiot?

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.460
Nothing, really...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.470
Are you thinking about that girl again?

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.220
No way.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.390
Hey!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.100
Why not talk to your older sister?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.560
That hurts! What're you talking about, being my fiancée?

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.180
How lucky...

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:04.730
I guess it's true that anyone's fine...

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.900
That's what your cousin said!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.020
I won't deny that...

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.030
The fireworks display...

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:16.160
She was looking forward to it.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.120
I was looking forward to it, too...

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.370
Hoping to go with you...

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.040
I see.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.580
Then, why don't we put on a little fireworks display?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:37.130
Rea-dono. Rea-dono, I really thank you for all the help you've given us.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.140
This little bit is fine.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.260
Yeah, but...

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.930
It is fine.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.480
What on earth is this?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.270
I'm sorry, Mero-chan.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:51.900
I'm home.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.280
Furuya-kun, welcome home.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.150
Nii, you are back early.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.450
What are you doing, cleaning in the middle of the day?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.410
And that broom...

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.950
I am fine.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.320
It's cloudy anyway.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.660
You worry too much.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.330
Really?

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.790
Really.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.170
Make sure you get proper rest afterwards.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.510
I will.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:18.840
Anyway, putting that aside, let's put on our own fireworks display.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.260
Fireworks display?

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:21.850
Yeah.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.720
Here tonight.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.390
We could launch bottle rockets and such.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.270
It has been a while since we have put on a display of fireworks.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.900
That sounds fun.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.980
Okay, it's decided.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.030
Ranko said that she'd lend you a yukata, so try it on.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.610
She'll help you get dressed, too.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.280
It's for the atmosphere, so let's do it properly.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.370
Is Ranko-san coming?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.330
She'll also bring the fireworks.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.910
I'll wear a yukata as well.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:48.870
See you.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.580
It'll start when Ranko gets here.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:55.050
I need to go and prepare dinner.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:55.920
Yeah.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.920
I'll clean this place up.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.460
I will leave it to you, then.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.390
See you.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.220
Ranko-san, huh?

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:27.870
Hello!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.530
Hi, Ranko-chan.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.410
Welcome.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.670
You're setting off fireworks, right?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.790
Yes!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.590
I feel bad about the fireworks display getting cancelled,

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.670
so I thought we could at least do it ourselves.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.460
Yo, Ranko.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.840
Oh, you can wear it pretty well too.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.800
Yeah.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.510
Mero helped me with it.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.930
It is nothing.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.350
I got used to it since I wear them everyday.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.850
So... Where's Rea-chan?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.270
Upstairs.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.190
Rea!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.410
Is it all right to tie your sash?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.330
It's totally fine!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.580
Actually, I'd like you to tie the sash tightly.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.630
I see.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:40.480
Ranko-san and Furuya-kun get along well, right?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:41.490
That's right.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.110
After all, we're childhood friends.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.820
He's been weird since he was young.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.780
At first, he annoyed me,

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.660
but he has a lot of good points.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.870
That's why I treasure him.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.620
I see.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:58.210
Normally, he wouldn't be interested in fireworks,

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.880
but when I suggested doing this, he was up for it.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.510
He's quite simple.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.880
He thought that Rea-chan would be happy about it.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.800
I don't know if he's a good or bad guy,

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.390
but in the end, I guess he's good.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.890
I guess I understand that a bit as well.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:14.890
All right!

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.230
It's done.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.650
Turn and look this way.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.940
Okay.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.400
It doesn't look out of place at all,

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.370
even though the person in front of me is actually a zombie.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.370
You're actually alive, right?

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.120
Of course not.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.790
I don't have a pulse.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.290
Other than the wound on your stomach, everything else is fine, right?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.040
I don't know how long this condition will last.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.420
I don't have much time left.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.340
My body is slowly decaying.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.260
Eh?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.350
Ranko-san?

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.390
It's totally fine, right?

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.270
Hydrangea, right?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.390
It's working properly, right?

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.190
I'm sure Chihiro will be able to do something about it.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:00.890
Yes.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.520
That's right.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.570
You can be here forever.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:07.650
No, I didn't mean I'd be here forever...

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.820
So, are you going somewhere else?

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:14.650
No, I'm not sure... I don't know...

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.870
U-Um...

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.710
Staying here forever would cause too much trouble...

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.090
I see...

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.710
He'd be lonely...

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.130
R-Really?

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.480
Um...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.840
Ranko-san...

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.400
Do you like...

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.900
I do.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:42.730
What about you?

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.610
Eh?

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.820
Me? I... um...

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.030
Something that huge...

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:51.910
Then isn't it fine for me to take Chihiro all for myself?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.450
Um...

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.500
That's...

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.250
That should be...

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.880
Rea-chan, are you worrying about me?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.550
W-What do you mean...

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.130
Geez, Rea-chan, you're so obvious.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:15.720
What I mean is that the two of us are "rivals"...

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:17.560
Um...

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.150
Not really.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:23.520
I'm not as close to Furuya-kun as you are...

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.820
And Furuya-kun only pays attention to me because I'm a zombie.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.240
For God's sake!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.950
Why are you holding back?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.620
Especially in your case!

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.280
If you think you don't have much time left,

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.950
then you have more reason to live without regrets.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.450
You're a girl!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.500
Ranko-san...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.000
I'm already dead, though.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.510
I'm not good at not being straight to the point.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:56.970
Even if Rea-chan likes Chihiro,

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.470
I am still me,

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.100
and you are you.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:04.100
However, I am not going to lose.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.070
So, Rea-chan, you do your best.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:10.900
Yes.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.340
Are you having fun?

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:37.550
I am.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:41.810
I'm sorry that this is all I can do.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:45.330
Furuya-kun, you're randomly apologising again.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.060
Well, that's...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.570
Don't worry about it.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.140
I am satisfied with being able to stay here.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.120
Isn't it boring?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:00.950
Not at all.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.290
Is there anything you're not happy about?

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.290
There's nothing.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.550
It's refreshing to be able to live here with Furuya-kun every day.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.170
It's exciting.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.400
Rather than having a huge fireworks display,

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.510
right now I think that this smaller one is much nicer.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.730
I'm home.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.940
W-Welcome home.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.240
What happened, Ojou-sama?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.030
I will go back to school.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.740
That's why I came back to get my stuff.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:40.990
That's not a problem, right?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.160
No...

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.170
Please inform her...

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.670
I will.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.030
Mother.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:20.950
Are you going back to school?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:21.990
Yes.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.540
That is what I have decided.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:27.910
How will you face going back to Danichirou-san's school?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.040
Are you going to expel me?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.250
No.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.380
Danichirou-san told me to do nothing.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.010
I won't do anything.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.930
Do what you want.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.550
Thank you very much.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:45.020
But I really won't do anything.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:48.270
I won't worry, I won't care, and I won't help.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.980
I am prepared.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.570
In that case, after you've done what
you need to do, get out of my house.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.530
Excuse me.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:19.970
Are you okay?

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:21.590
Yes.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.600
Thanks, Furuya-kun.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.600
About school...

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.190
You want to go, right?

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.310
Yes.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.900
Is it really okay?

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.690
It's fine.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.320
It can't be helped.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.320
I'm very happy.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:44.570
If I cannot go to school, then how can I be considered a normal girl?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:47.080
I was a bit lonely.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.080
So something is troubling you.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.580
Something troubling me...

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.830
I guess you're right. I'm sorry.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:01.590
But promise me that you'll be careful.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.590
I will.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:07.260
Let's do our best to protect your body.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.600
Right.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.610
I...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:22.360
Yes?

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.570
...want to be honest about something...

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.580
Please do.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:32.370
I want you to stay like this for as long as possible.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:38.290
Can I also be honest with you about something?

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.210
Sure.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.470
I don't want to have any regrets.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:48.930
Since I don't know when I will disappear, I want to do as much as I can.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.730
That's because I'm a girl.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.030
It can't be helped.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.990
I guess it can't be helped.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.320
That's right.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.660
That's right!

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.920
My happiness is built upon Rea's misfortune,

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:15.670
and Rea's happiness is built upon mine.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.960
I understand.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.670
Even though I get it,

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.670
but...

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:23.630
If you're going to school,

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:27.300
we should put some dry ice inside that coat.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.930
But you'd only wear the coat when you're going to and coming back from school.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:33.100
And you can't wear it during the summer.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:36.730
Anyway, wouldn't it be weird to wear a coat during the summer?

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.480
What do you think?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.230
But at that moment,

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:45.780
I...

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:49.870
At that moment, I...

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:54.200
...realised that I can share my happiness and misfortunes with Rea.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:57.920
At that moment...

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:42.630
Next time.

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:47.390
Sankarea 13: I am... a Zombie, too...

00:23:47.390 --> 00:23:49.320
Everyone watch it!

00:23:55.570 --> 00:24:00.510
I do not believe I could have made it this far on my own.

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:03.160
I cannot help but express my gratitude.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.630
Thank you...

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:07.660
Truly, thank you.
